{
  "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
  "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nDEANNE E. MAYNARD, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner in No. 15-1039.\nANTHONY A. YANG, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner in No. 15-1039.\nSETH P. WAXMAN, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners in No. 15-1195."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sandoz, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Biosimilars Act created a comprehensive and self-contained scheme for the early resolution of patent disputes. Regardless of the actions an applicant or sponsor take along the way, the end result is the same, patent litigation. Courts should apply that comprehensive scheme as written. They shouldn't look elsewhere for consequences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could you tell me, suppose that in year 2 of the 12-year exclusive period, the application for the biosimilar is made. And then in year 4, there is eight more years to run, the commission -- the FDA decides that it's going to approve it. Is it licensed at that time?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sandoz, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute provides powerful incentives for the sponsors to continue through the process, Justice Sotomayor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can you explain the difference -- there are two rounds of patent infringement; right? Round 1 and -- can you explain the difference between those two?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Anthony A. Yang",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YANG: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Congress enacted a detailed process for early resolution of patent disputes through patent infringement litigation while FDA is evaluating a biosimilar application. The statute expressly establishes a series of procedural steps, and then specifies the consequences for both the applicant and the sponsor if they fail to take the steps that would set you off the -- the (l) path."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Anthony A. Yang",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0001-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Those consequences, which are quite detailed -- we don't have the time to talk about all of them, but they're in the statute, they're in our brief -- are the exclusive consequences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But even if it did, the reason why Congress -- the reason why you have to have FDA -- the FDA say what's being approved, whereas in Hatch-Waxman you don't, is in Hatch-Waxman we are talking about a small molecule that has to be identical. It's made by chemical synthesis, so there's no question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, if -- in fact, if you look again, we're on the 180-day notice provision, subsection (a) of 262(l)(8), which -- I'm sorry, I'm looking at my own appendix, but it's on page 31A of -- of my appendix."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that (8)(a) notice, first and foremost, allows the sponsor, for the very first time, to seek a preliminary injunction against the commercial marketing of the product for the uses using the processes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so in some of them, there have -- you know, for example, Amgen got approved -- biosimilar approval for its biosimilar to AbbVie's referenced drug Humira."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. Waxman, let's say -- let's say I spot you that, okay, that (2)(A) \"shall\" means shall. All right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the litigation -- the complaint in this case asked for an order under the California statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ALL RIGHT? So if you don't invoke the Federal process, what remains? That's not a remedy. That's a different Federal process, the declaratory-judgment process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Not to prejudge the issues, maybe."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- what (8)(A) says is, you can't file a declaratory-judgment action until you get the notice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But even in that instance, number one, under (l) -- the statute in (l)(7) recognizes that the sponsor may well obtain other patents after the lists are exchanged."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "and that's what the 180 days does -- to allow the parties to say even with respect to the phase I patents, we now have a real dispute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There can be no doubt that the judgment that we've petitioned on is a Federal judgment. The -- the Federal Circuit issued a Federal injunction and dismissed their State law claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amgen",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yet, Amgen wants you to read the statute and to read those -- the rest of these provisions as implicitly entitling them to an injunction that Congress chose not to provide, and instead they want to call the remedies Congress did provide as the backup."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5da794bcd5ea-0003-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress provided consequences. If they decide not to sue, then they can only get a reasonable royalty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1039",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "5da794bcd5ea2f5347218c7ef1150a1c0eaab8e7739eacfc9d060c2dd18d1e2e",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-5da794bcd5ea-64",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
